{
 "about": "Reiners et al. 2016 (A&A 587, A65; Table 2 and Sect. 3) co-add 1190 VIS scans from nine days of 2014, in packages of 10 scans taking ~15 min, each package shifted by the Sun-observer radial velocity (JPL Horizons) into the solar frame before averaging. So each package's telluric lines sit at -v_r in the atlas, and v_r moves by 0.6 km/s between April and July and by +-0.2 km/s within a day. The paper gives the scans per day but not when they were taken. Each day's packages are put back to back, centred on the Sun's transit at G\u00f6ttingen, and that stretch is cut into hour-long nodes (at least one), each weighted by its share of the day's scans, with its own air mass and v_r at its midpoint. Each day gets the ERA5 profile at 11 UTC (transit is at ~11:20 UTC on these dates):",
 "source": "Reiners et al. 2016, A&A 587, A65, Table 2 (VIS)",
